@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix gufo:    <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/dreaming>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Dreaming Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Dreaming Module — a published extension-tier composition over the experiential/mentation layer: dreams, dream reports, and dream elements are built from gmeow:Experience, gmeow:AwarenessMode, gmeow:ContentOrigin, gmeow:LearningEvent, gmeow:Analogy, and metacognition with no new primitives."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/dreaming> ;
    rdfs:comment """The dreaming slice is a pure composition over core GMEOW occurrent and awareness machinery. No new primitives are minted.

DREAM COMPOSITION.
  * A dream is an instance of gmeow:Experience with:
      - gmeow:mentalProcessType gmeow:processDreaming
      - gmeow:awarenessMode value gmeow:modeDreaming or gmeow:modeREM
      - gmeow:contentOrigin gmeow:originImagined
  * Lucid dreaming = the same composition but with gmeow:awarenessMode gmeow:modeLucidDreaming.
  * Memory-consolidation dreaming = an offline gmeow:LearningEvent with gmeow:learningType gmeow:learningConsolidation, recombining stored claims via gmeow:Analogy and gmeow:learningConceptFormation.

DOCTRINE.
  * No new primitives (Principle 4 / Principle 6): this slice adds only gmeow:DreamReport and gmeow:dreamElement. Every dream kind is composed from existing core classes and value vocabularies; the dream itself is a composed gmeow:Experience, the dream report is a composed recollection gmeow:Experience, and dream elements are linked through one new object property whose domain is gmeow:Experience and whose range stays open.
  * Composition, not taxonomy: no subclassing of gmeow:Experience beyond what the mentation slice already allows. Finer dream kinds (lucid, REM, consolidation, recurring) are value-tagged or restriction-typed compositions, never subclasses of gmeow:Experience.
  * Co-equal vantage-indexed claims (Principle 9 / Principle 10): a dream report is a low-reliability recollection; competing reports, analyst interpretations, elementations, and lucidity attributions coexist as standpoint-indexed claims, with superseded claims suppressed by gmeow:displayable false rather than deleted."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> .

# =========================================================================== #
# DREAM REPORT — recollection of a dream, treated as a low-reliability claim
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:DreamReport
    a owl:Class, gufo:EventType ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Experience ;
    rdfs:label "Dream Report"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A recollection experience in which an agent reports or recalls a dream — a gmeow:Experience whose mental-process kind is gmeow:processRecollection and whose content originates in imagination (gmeow:contentOrigin gmeow:originImagined). A standpoint-indexed, low-metacognitive-reliability claim: competing reports coexist and superseded reports are suppressed, not deleted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:comment """A dream report is a recollection episode: an instance of gmeow:Experience with gmeow:mentalProcessType gmeow:processRecollection and gmeow:contentOrigin gmeow:originImagined. It is a claim about a prior dream episode, but modelled as the recollection process itself rather than as a propositional claim class, so it inherits the occurrent mental-timeline machinery (gmeow:experiencer, gmeow:mentalProcessType, etc.) from gmeow:Experience.

Dream reports are co-equal vantage-indexed claims with low metacognitive reliability (Principle 9): the dreamer, an analyst, and a later interview may produce competing reports of the same dream episode, and all may coexist. A superseded report (for example, a corrected or withdrawn dream-journal entry) is suppressed with gmeow:displayable false rather than deleted (Principle 10)."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty gmeow:mentalProcessType ; owl:hasValue gmeow:processRecollection ] ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty gmeow:contentOrigin ; owl:hasValue gmeow:originImagined ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/dreaming> .

# =========================================================================== #
# DREAM ELEMENT — imagined constituent of a dream
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:dreamElement
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:Experience ;
    rdfs:label "dream element"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a dream or other imagined experiential episode to one of its imagined constituents — a figure, object, place, event, or proposition occurring within the dream. Range intentionally OPEN: the element may be any entity the dreamer or analyst wishes to identify. NOT functional: a dream contains many elements."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:comment """Used to decompose a dream experience into its constituent imagined parts. The range is deliberately left open (Principle 13) so the property can point at any entity, description, or proposition that plays a part in the dream. Competing elementations from different vantages coexist as co-equal claims (Principle 9)."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/dreaming> .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Graph box role coverage (canonical explicit annotations).
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/dreaming> gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox, gmeow:boxTBox .
gmeow:DreamReport gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
gmeow:dreamElement gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .
